olves  around her she gets in between Joker and  the kechi at times and seemingly  confronts the moral quandary zuv what it  means to be a phantom thief as to the  extent to which these themes are  explored with Qasimi we'll have to wait  and see because one I haven't spoiled it  for myself and two I wouldn't spoil it  for you either one of the best parts of  persona 5 was the virtual tourism of  Tokyo taking a page out of the Yakuza  series playbook in the original game we  got  shibuya shinjuku Akihabara and more in  p5 R we have a new location within Tokyo  to hit up kiichi Choji in real life QT  GOG is a part of town with shops  restaurants and places to hang out in p5  are it's kind of like that too what  makes this place special is that there  are new group activities as you can  chill at penguins sniper a spot to shoot  pool and play darts with the squad now  why would you want to do this these  activities level up baton pass ranks  with the team adding special perks to  this clutch combat mechanic different  spots open up at night in keachi Choji -  there's a jazz club you can take your  friends - and a shrine to visit that  helps boost your stats now when it comes  to combat and exploration in the  Metaverse p5 are does some remix in  palaces have additional areas to explore  slightly changing the original layouts  Joker's new grappling hook ability is a  means to get too many of these nooks and  crannies performed as contact sensitive  actions the grappling hook will also be  a way of ambushing enemies from a  distance but it's my understanding that  it unlocks through a confidante perk  boss battles have changed slightly with  new phases fighting the first boss calm  Ishida in the demo I saw an Adam  mechanic where he summons cognitive  versions of Mishima and Shiho  I'm so sorry chica mashita I have a  rehear they affect the battle with  different attacks but you ultimately  need to inflict damage on them or , she  notes and move past this phase it didn'